WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.390
Speaker 1: Well, I have an opportunity today
to do two things that I think are valuable.

00:00:04.390 --> 00:00:09.000
One is debunk a false talking point that is
spreading like wildfire.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:13.870
And number two, to remind everybody that the
entire Tulsi Gabbard thing was a complete

00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:15.059
and total scam.

00:00:15.059 --> 00:00:16.880
Tulsi Gabbard Who?

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:22.280
So I guess somebody I thought was on the left
at one point when she ran for president and

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:29.910
when she was a Democrat, she continues to
provide a reactionary takes on Fox News.

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:35.100
And last night, she provided a reactionary
take that is a great opportunity to explain

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:40.170
reality to her and to people in the audience
and to make sure that we're all equipped with

00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:43.460
the truth about this question.

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:47.969
Did the Supreme Court leaker commit a crime?

00:00:47.969 --> 00:00:54.909
Because for all the talk about due process
that the right claims to support, they are

00:00:54.909 --> 00:01:01.829
increasingly demanding the prosecution and
imprisonment of the Supreme Court leaker absent

00:01:01.829 --> 00:01:06.820
any actual crime that we can point to that
they committed.

00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:09.110
So let's start with Tulsi.

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:15.290
You might be shocked that Tulsi appeared to
express outrage.

00:01:15.290 --> 00:01:17.400
That the decision leaked.

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:23.760
Not that women's autonomy will now be allowed
to be restricted by states.

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:27.460
She was outraged that we learned about this
three weeks early.

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:28.460
Let's take a listen.

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:29.500
Speaker 5: To be heard.

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:35.230
I think it's also critical to point out that
this leak sets a very, very dangerous precedent

00:01:35.230 --> 00:01:38.340
for our Supreme Court for three important
reasons.

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:43.850
Number one is, first of all, this person is
a thief who stole this information, released

00:01:43.850 --> 00:01:48.910
it with a very specific intent to try to incite
protesters and intimidate and pressure our

00:01:48.910 --> 00:01:54.520
Supreme Court justices to make a political
decision rather than a decision that is based

00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:56.700
on the Constitution.

00:01:56.700 --> 00:02:02.850
Number two, we have the fact that Supreme
Court is not in place to legislate from the

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:04.170
bench people's representatives.

00:02:04.170 --> 00:02:07.290
Speaker 1: And yet that's exactly what they're
doing with this decision.

00:02:07.290 --> 00:02:10.819
Speaker 5: State level at the federal level
are charged to make laws, not the Supreme

00:02:10.819 --> 00:02:11.819
Court.

00:02:11.819 --> 00:02:14.670
The Supreme Court needs to make decisions
based on the Constitution.

00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:20.049
And the Department of Justice, lastly, needs
to go and prosecute this crime, which is exactly

00:02:20.049 --> 00:02:23.620
what it is, and make an example out of the
person who leaked this information.

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:27.879
Because our Supreme Court justices cannot
operate under the fear that they will have

00:02:27.879 --> 00:02:34.269
partizan political activists in their house
intimidating and threatening their ability

00:02:34.269 --> 00:02:36.189
to do their job per the Constitution.

00:02:36.189 --> 00:02:41.790
Speaker 1: Okay, so Tulsi uses the word thief
and that sounds criminal.

00:02:41.790 --> 00:02:44.499
I don't know if theft is illegal, right?

00:02:44.499 --> 00:02:47.160
But it wasn't that we know of a crime.

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:49.150
So that's one thing I'm going to talk about.

00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:56.439
The second piece of this is she insists that
this was someone who didn't like the forthcoming

00:02:56.439 --> 00:03:01.810
decision to overturn Roe v Wade, meaning it's
presumably someone on the left who leaked

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:06.319
this in order to try to pressure the justices
to change their minds.

00:03:06.319 --> 00:03:11.370
And sometime between now and whenever the
decision comes out, decide to preserve Roe

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:12.370
v Wade.

00:03:12.370 --> 00:03:13.569
I'll get to that part in a second.

00:03:13.569 --> 00:03:15.750
So let's start with the crime piece.

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:20.549
This is not about your opinion of whether
it was good or bad that this leaked three

00:03:20.549 --> 00:03:21.730
weeks early.

00:03:21.730 --> 00:03:27.889
I just want to talk about whether it's a crime
if to get to this document.

00:03:27.889 --> 00:03:33.310
Someone at the Supreme Court hacked a computer
they weren't supposed to have access to, physically

00:03:33.310 --> 00:03:35.439
trespassed somewhere.

00:03:35.439 --> 00:03:36.810
That could be a crime.

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:41.670
We have no evidence of any hacking or trespassing
right now.

00:03:41.670 --> 00:03:46.650
Secondly, Supreme Court draft decisions are
not classified.

00:03:46.650 --> 00:03:50.529
That's another angle where this is this this
must be like a classified document.

00:03:50.529 --> 00:03:51.529
It's not.

00:03:51.529 --> 00:03:53.890
So there's no crime there either.

00:03:53.890 --> 00:03:59.169
If I want to be as charitable as possible
and say, where could there be a crime here

00:03:59.169 --> 00:04:06.249
under the loosest interpretation possible,
you could maybe be charged with stealing federal

00:04:06.249 --> 00:04:09.629
government property for your own use.

00:04:09.629 --> 00:04:13.769
It's extraordinarily unlikely that you would
see that it's not even clear that it would

00:04:13.769 --> 00:04:15.250
necessarily fit.

00:04:15.250 --> 00:04:22.961
Now, if an investigation starts and authorities
interview anyone, the leaker or whoever, and

00:04:22.961 --> 00:04:28.000
you lie to them, okay, that's a crime that
would be making a federal false statement

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:29.430
charge.

00:04:29.430 --> 00:04:30.440
But that's an if.

00:04:30.440 --> 00:04:31.440
Okay.

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:34.419
So there's no crime that we're aware of here.

00:04:34.419 --> 00:04:36.740
So why would anybody be prosecuted and locked
up?

00:04:36.740 --> 00:04:39.759
Because that's what people like to see another
reactionaries are calling for.

00:04:39.759 --> 00:04:40.759
Now, one other thing.

00:04:40.759 --> 00:04:45.199
If the leaker is a lawyer, they could be subject
to an ethics probe.

00:04:45.199 --> 00:04:46.849
They could be subject to being disbarred.

00:04:46.849 --> 00:04:49.800
These aren't crimes, but they could lose their
law license.

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:51.330
Bottom line firing?

00:04:51.330 --> 00:04:52.330
Sure.

00:04:52.330 --> 00:04:53.330
Disbarment.

00:04:53.330 --> 00:04:54.330
If a lawyer.

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:55.330
Sure.

00:04:55.330 --> 00:04:56.330
Crime?

00:04:56.330 --> 00:04:57.330
Almost certainly not.

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:58.330
No evidence of that at this point in time.

00:04:58.330 --> 00:05:06.759
Second part, they continue to assume these
right wingers that the leaker is a pro-choice

00:05:06.759 --> 00:05:14.250
left winger, angry with the forthcoming decision
to overturn Roe v Wade, releasing this draft

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:20.099
in order to try to put public pressure on
the justices planning to vote in favor of

00:05:20.099 --> 00:05:21.830
overturning Roe v Wade.

00:05:21.830 --> 00:05:27.020
So they will be scared and they'll change
their mind and they will vote to keep Roe

00:05:27.020 --> 00:05:28.290
v Wade.

00:05:28.290 --> 00:05:33.389
First of all, lifetime appointments, extremely
good security.

00:05:33.389 --> 00:05:38.229
I don't even think it passes the sniff test
that it would work if that's what the plan

00:05:38.229 --> 00:05:42.470
was to intimidate the justices planning to
vote to overturn.

00:05:42.470 --> 00:05:48.470
But I actually have another perspective here,
which is we're we're only speculating we don't

00:05:48.470 --> 00:05:50.379
know who the leaker is.

00:05:50.379 --> 00:05:54.139
The leaker could just as likely be a right
winger.

00:05:54.139 --> 00:05:55.740
Who leaked this.

00:05:55.740 --> 00:06:01.430
In order to try to lock in the justices in
sticking with their decision to overturn Roe

00:06:01.430 --> 00:06:02.430
v Wade.

00:06:02.430 --> 00:06:09.970
In other words, a right winger might say there
might be justices who in this February draft

00:06:09.970 --> 00:06:12.870
wanted to vote to overturn Roe v Wade.

00:06:12.870 --> 00:06:15.120
But now maybe because it's May.

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:18.930
Now, remember, this person might know what
happened since the draft is written.

00:06:18.930 --> 00:06:24.530
Maybe the leaker is a right winger, doesn't
like abortion and says, Wow, I found out that

00:06:24.530 --> 00:06:25.530
I don't know.

00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:29.080
Gorsuch is thinking about actually voting
to keep Roe v Wade.

00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:34.780
I am going to leak this to make their names
public so that they are less likely to change

00:06:34.780 --> 00:06:39.780
their vote because that would potentially
cause some kind of uproar or whatever.

00:06:39.780 --> 00:06:42.409
The point is, we don't know either way right
now.

00:06:42.409 --> 00:06:43.780
At some point we might.

00:06:43.780 --> 00:06:45.010
Right now we don't know.

00:06:45.010 --> 00:06:49.479
And all of this is completely irresponsible,
particularly saying that people who have not

00:06:49.479 --> 00:06:53.500
committed any crime that we're aware of or
that can be articulated should be prosecuted

00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:56.610
and put in prison, as so many like Ted Cruz
have been demanding

